olivia park: Customer (FinEdge) asked for a 2-week POC: streaming results (render rows as they arrive), tool/function calls to their payments API, and a pricing quote for steady 50k tokens/day. Also attached a security questionnaire.
matthew jones: Quick questions: do they expect each streamed chunk to be a complete JSON object, or are we allowed to send NDJSON fragments that the client stitches?
nina rao: They said "streamed JSON rows" but unclear about array vs lines. Recommend NDJSON over websocket/SSE; easiest for progressive render and robust on partial network.
olivia park: They also need a demo of function/tool calling: payments.lookup(account_id) that returns balance + transaction_count. Can we show consistent ordering so a row with tool result maps to the correct UI row?
matthew jones: We emit messages sequentially; include an "id" field for correlation. Example chunk: {"type":"row","id":42,"payload":{"text":"..."}} then {"type":"tool_result","id":42,"payload":{"balance":123.45}}. Ordering preserved by stream.
harry_sales: Procurement asked for two price options: hosted trial (30 days) and dedicated 3-month POC. Needs ballpark numbers + note about commit min.
olivia park: Matt/Finance please send ranges. Also we need to confirm timeline: hosted demo can be ready in 3 days if FinEdge shares sample dataset and API spec. Private/VPC POC ~10 business days for infra and KMS BYOK.
nina rao: Security checklist summary: SOC2 yes, SAML SSO supported, IP allowlist, audit logs, KMS BYOK on Private. For hosted trial we can provide isolated project + audit logs and ephemeral keys. If they insist on BYOK, must use Private.
ops-bot: env-create request queued: finedge-hosted-demo (ETA 72h)
matthew jones: SDK snippet for Node (minimal) to include in SOW:
```js
const s = await Redwood.stream.connect({key:process.env.RW_KEY});
s.on('message', raw => {
  const msg = JSON.parse(raw);
  if(msg.type === 'row') renderRow(msg.id, msg.payload);
  if(msg.type === 'tool_result') applyToolResult(msg.id, msg.payload);
});
// initiate tool call
s.send(JSON.stringify({type:'tool_call',id:42,name:'payments.lookup',args:{account_id:'A-123'}}));
```
olivia park: Add note: use structured_output_schema to enforce fields and types; it reduces parsing ambiguity and helps frontend validation.
harry_sales: Finance notes? We need hosted ~ $0.003/token estimate for high-quality model (trial discount possible). Dedicated POC starts at $20k/month pool for small infra; effective token price ~30-45% lower depending on commit. I'll get firm numbers.
matthew jones: Frontend caveat: some browsers break on very large single-line NDJSON flushes. Recommend chunk size ~1-2KB per message or use smaller logical rows. Also provide heartbeat frames to keep connections alive.
nina rao: For SAML we'll need their IdP metadata and ACS URL. For KMS BYOK: key ARN + rotation policy. Ops needs least-privilege access to attach keys.
olivia park: Action items: 1) Matt to draft hosted + dedicated pricing ranges and send spreadsheet (EOD). 2) Nina to produce 1-page security summary for SOW (tomorrow). 3) Matt + Nina to prepare the hosted POC runbook and the Node snippet updated with structured_output_schema (48h). 4) Harry to request security questionnaire answers and preferred start date from FinEdge.
harry_sales: On it. I'll ask for sample dataset + API swagger and confirm start date next Monday.
ops-bot: ephemeral keys created: rw-ephemeral-9a2c (valid 72h)
olivia park: Great. Keep updates here and paste final SDK snippet in the SOW. :thumbsup:
